1
00:00:08,021 --> 00:00:11,894
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

2
00:00:12,908 --> 00:00:20,233
One story that was mentioned to us in Qur'an, gives us an impression about the Hawariyyeen(حواريّين).

3
00:00:21,293 --> 00:00:24,001
And the Hawariyyeen(حواريّين) are the Sahabah(صحابه) of Sayidina Eesa(سيدنا عيسى).

4
00:00:24,981 --> 00:00:28,955
The followers or the companions of Sayidina Muhammadﷺ were called Sahabah(صحابه).

5
00:00:29,528 --> 00:00:33,209
The Companions of Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام were called Al-Hawariyyeen(الحواريّين).

6
00:00:33,776 --> 00:00:35,209
In English; The disciples.

7
00:00:36,376 --> 00:00:38,320
These Ayaat(آيات) are in Surat ul Maidah(سورةالمائدة).

8
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:44,935
And Al-Maidah(المائدة) is named after these Ayaat(آيات); because Al-Maidah(المائدة) means; a table.

9
00:00:46,169 --> 00:00:47,582
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

10
00:00:47,969 --> 00:00:58,790
إِذْ قَالَ الْحَوَارِيُّونَ يَا عِيسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ هَلْ يَسْتَطِيعُ رَبُّكَ أَن يُنَزِّلَ عَلَيْنَا مَائِدَةً مِّنَ السَّمَاءِ ۖ

11
00:00:58,863 --> 00:01:04,723
 Remember! When Al-Hawariyyeen(الحواريّين); The disciples said, Oh Eesa(عيسى)! And Eesa(عيسى) is Jesus.

12
00:01:05,263 --> 00:01:12,543
And by the way, the name Eesa(عيسى) is closer to the right pronunciation of his real name, than Jesus is.

13
00:01:12,583 --> 00:01:19,445
Because, in the Aramaic language of Sayidina Eesa(سيدنا عيسى) and the people of Sayidina Eesa(سيدنا عيسى), the letter ''J'' did not exist.

14
00:01:20,605 --> 00:01:23,765
So the name Jesus isn't truly his name.

15
00:01:24,225 --> 00:01:30,740
His name is Eesa(عيسى) or at least it's a closer pronunciation of the name of Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام.

16
00:01:31,260 --> 00:01:32,986
But in English; now it's called Jesus.

17
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:40,403
They said; Can your Lord send down to us a table spread with food from heaven?

18
00:01:40,936 --> 00:01:45,456
So the companions, Al-Hawariyyeen(الحواريّين), and we'll use the name Al-Hawariyyeen(الحواريّين) from now on, the disciples.

19
00:01:45,556 --> 00:01:52,922
Al-Hawariyyeen(الحواريّين); they came to Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام, and they said; Can your Lord send us a table?

20
00:01:53,549 --> 00:01:56,468
Now, if this question means; Is Allah able to do so?

21
00:01:56,888 --> 00:01:57,908
Then this is Kuffr(كفر).

22
00:01:58,828 --> 00:02:01,814
What do you mean, Allah is not able to bring down a table from the sky?

23
00:02:02,301 --> 00:02:04,290
You're doubting the ability of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

24
00:02:04,390 --> 00:02:06,477
Can Allah bring down the table? Of course, Allah can.

25
00:02:07,490 --> 00:02:09,215
Is that the meaning they intended?

26
00:02:09,629 --> 00:02:13,582
According to some scholars; yes, but the majority say; that's not what they intended.

27
00:02:14,229 --> 00:02:17,624
Especially, when we know in Qur'an Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says about Al-Hawariyyeen(الحواريّين).

28
00:02:17,837 --> 00:02:19,184
Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام said;

29
00:02:19,224 --> 00:02:20,397
مَنْ أَنصَارِي إِلَى اللَّهِ ۖ

30
00:02:20,611 --> 00:02:23,287
Who are my supporters in the sake of Allah?

31
00:02:23,567 --> 00:02:25,420
قَالَ الْحَوَارِيُّونَ نَحْنُ أَنصَارُ اللَّهِ

32
00:02:25,807 --> 00:02:31,786
The Hawariyyeen(حواريّين) said; we are going to be the ones who will give victory to the religion of Allah.

33
00:02:32,173 --> 00:02:34,306
آمَنَّا بِاللَّهِ وَاشْهَدْ بِأَنَّا مُسْلِمُونَ۝

34
00:02:34,366 --> 00:02:37,816
We believed in Allah and be a witness that we are Muslims.

35
00:02:38,642 --> 00:02:45,199
So this Ayah(آية) gives us an indication that, the that the followers of Sayidina Eesa(سيدنا عيسى) were firm believers, who believed in him,

36
00:02:45,279 --> 00:02:48,157
and believed in Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, and believed in Islam.

37
00:02:48,704 --> 00:02:52,392
So we cannot expect from them to come to Eesa(عيسى) and ask him;

38
00:02:52,466 --> 00:02:58,118
Can Allah bring down a table, as if they're questioning the ability of Allah to do so.

39
00:02:58,584 --> 00:03:00,011
So what does this Ayah(آية) means?

40
00:03:00,318 --> 00:03:07,794
The scholars say that, what they meant by this question is; is it possible for you to ask Allah to bring down a table for us?

41
00:03:08,947 --> 00:03:10,055
Can Allah bring down a table?

42
00:03:10,101 --> 00:03:12,595
So they're asking him; can Allah do this for us?

43
00:03:13,068 --> 00:03:15,341
Is it something that you can ask Allah to do for us?

44
00:03:15,841 --> 00:03:16,867
You get the meaning.

45
00:03:17,367 --> 00:03:18,980
There are two different things.

46
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:22,643
But again; it's not something that the Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ did.

47
00:03:23,276 --> 00:03:27,348
The followers of Muhammadﷺ never requested Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to send down a miracle.

48
00:03:27,708 --> 00:03:28,288
Never!

49
00:03:29,655 --> 00:03:35,575
Never did any one of the companions; The Sahabahرضى الله عنهم come to Rasool Allah ﷺ and say; Perform for us a miracle; Never!

50
00:03:35,748 --> 00:03:36,575
They never did it.

51
00:03:37,735 --> 00:03:43,979
So the Hawariyyeen(حواريّين); they did come to Eesa(عيسى), and they asked for a miracle.

52
00:03:44,232 --> 00:03:46,066
Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام said;

53
00:03:46,111 --> 00:03:46,665
اتَّقُوا اللَّهَ

54
00:03:46,745 --> 00:03:47,705
Fear Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

55
00:03:47,725 --> 00:03:48,878
Why are you asking me to do so?

56
00:03:49,265 --> 00:03:51,478
اتَّقُوا اللَّهَ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ۝

57
00:03:51,778 --> 00:03:54,286
Fear Allah, if you are indeed believer.

58
00:03:54,733 --> 00:03:56,893
They gave their justifications.

59
00:03:57,493 --> 00:03:58,133
They said;

60
00:03:58,966 --> 00:04:01,283
قَالُواْ نُرِيدُ أَن نَّأْكُلَ مِنْهَا

61
00:04:01,623 --> 00:04:04,643
They said; We wish to eat, thereof.

62
00:04:05,156 --> 00:04:09,092
They might have been very hungry, and they wanted Rizq(رزق) from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

63
00:04:09,112 --> 00:04:11,252
And it's okay to ask for Rizq(رزق) from Allah.

64
00:04:11,565 --> 00:04:14,191
وَتَطْمَئِنَّ قُلُوبُنَا

65
00:04:14,911 --> 00:04:17,491
And to satisfy our hearts.

66
00:04:18,444 --> 00:04:21,308
When we see miracle, it will satisfy our hearts.

67
00:04:21,575 --> 00:04:24,282
It will make our Eeman(ايمان); firmer and stronger.

68
00:04:24,982 --> 00:04:25,975
So that's number two.

69
00:04:26,255 --> 00:04:28,244
وَنَعْلَمَ أَن قَدْ صَدَقْتَنَا

70
00:04:28,870 --> 00:04:32,604
And to know that you have indeed told us the truth.

71
00:04:33,504 --> 00:04:39,279
And again; you can see here a little bit of a difference again between the Sahabah(صحابه) of Muhammadﷺ and Hawariyyeen(حواريّين).

72
00:04:39,519 --> 00:04:43,107
The are saying; we want to see this, to make sure that you have told us the truth.

73
00:04:43,960 --> 00:04:46,053
وَنَكُونَ عَلَيْهَا مِنَ ٱلشَّٰهِدِينَ۝

74
00:04:46,533 --> 00:04:49,813
And that, we ourselves be its witnesses.

75
00:04:49,933 --> 00:04:52,886
Now even though, they made this the last justification.

76
00:04:52,926 --> 00:04:56,712
It should have been the first; because it has the strongest foundation.

77
00:04:57,112 --> 00:04:58,845
They said; we want to be witnesses.

78
00:04:59,505 --> 00:05:06,098
In other words, they're asking Sayidina Eesa(سيدنا عيسى) to perform this miracles in front of their eyes,

79
00:05:06,438 --> 00:05:11,511
so that, they can be witnesses in front of mankind; to say that we have seen this miracle with our eyes.

80
00:05:12,338 --> 00:05:16,781
So when they go in Da'wah(دعوة), and when they go to convey the message of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى;

81
00:05:17,021 --> 00:05:24,233
they can tell the people that, we have seen Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) performed this miracle in front of our eyes;

82
00:05:24,313 --> 00:05:25,593
وَنَكُونَ عَلَيْهَا مِنَ ٱلشَّٰهِدِينَ۝

83
00:05:25,613 --> 00:05:29,046
We will witness that, we will be witnesses in front of mankind.

84
00:05:29,366 --> 00:05:33,995
They convinced Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام with the validity of their request.

85
00:05:34,635 --> 00:05:36,195
Jesus, son of Mary said;

86
00:05:36,595 --> 00:05:49,148
قَالَ عِيسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ اللَّهُمَّ رَبَّنَا أَنزِلْ عَلَيْنَا مَائِدَةً مِّنَ السَّمَاءِ تَكُونُ لَنَا عِيدًا لِّأَوَّلِنَا وَآخِررِنَا

87
00:05:49,208 --> 00:05:51,854
Eesa(عيسى); Jesus; son of Mary said;

88
00:05:52,180 --> 00:05:57,902
Oh Allah, our Lord! Send us from the heaven a table spread with food.

89
00:05:58,496 --> 00:06:04,674
Now, when Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام made a Dua(دُعَا), and he was telling Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, why he wants the table.

90
00:06:05,100 --> 00:06:09,714
He did not use the same four justifications that Al-Hawariyyeen(الحواريّين) used.

91
00:06:10,374 --> 00:06:11,231
But he said;

92
00:06:12,591 --> 00:06:17,228
تَكُونُ لَنَا عِيدًا لِّأَوَّلِنَا وَآخِرِنَا

93
00:06:18,435 --> 00:06:22,866
Maybe for us a festival for the first and the last of us.

94
00:06:23,473 --> 00:06:25,326
Eesa(عيسى) said; send down this table.

95
00:06:26,493 --> 00:06:28,659
So that number one; it would be Eid(عيد) for us.

96
00:06:28,712 --> 00:06:29,819
What does Eid(عيد) mean?

97
00:06:30,552 --> 00:06:35,918
Eid(عيد) is a festival; but if we look at the linguistic meaning of the word Eid(عيد); Min Ya'ud(من يعود).

98
00:06:36,938 --> 00:06:40,317
Eid(عيد) in Arabic; it would mean; something that returns.

99
00:06:40,717 --> 00:06:42,030
It returns again and again.

100
00:06:42,217 --> 00:06:44,097
It would mean; something that is good.

101
00:06:44,270 --> 00:06:46,213
So why do we say Eid(عيد) a celebration?

102
00:06:46,473 --> 00:06:50,642
Because it's something that comes on a yearly basis like, Eid-ul-Fitr(عيدالفطر) and Eid-ul-Adha(عيدالاضحى),

103
00:06:50,862 --> 00:06:53,942
or it comes on a weekly basis like, Al-Jumu'ah(جُمعه).

104
00:06:54,188 --> 00:06:58,076
And it's a moment of celebration, a good moment, a pleasurable moment.

105
00:06:58,249 --> 00:06:59,963
So we wanted to come again and again.

106
00:07:00,449 --> 00:07:04,139
Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام wanted this to be Eid(عيد) for them.

107
00:07:04,286 --> 00:07:06,979
So that, they would remember the blessing of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

108
00:07:07,472 --> 00:07:11,351
Just as Eid-ul-Fitr(عيدالفطر) for example, is a celebration for us

109
00:07:11,391 --> 00:07:17,263
because we have completed the fasting of the month of Ramadan(رمضان), and now we are breaking our fast.

110
00:07:17,730 --> 00:07:19,110
And that's why, Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

111
00:07:19,130 --> 00:07:20,597
لصائم فرحتان

112
00:07:21,023 --> 00:07:26,556
For the person who's fasting has two moments of happiness; once when they break their fasting,

113
00:07:26,769 --> 00:07:30,316
and once on the day of judgment when they see the reward of their fasting.

114
00:07:31,169 --> 00:07:33,496
Sayidina Eesa(سيدنا عيسى) said; we want this to be Eid(عيد) for us.

115
00:07:35,642 --> 00:07:36,269
And then he said;

116
00:07:36,289 --> 00:07:37,289
وَآيَةً مِّنكَ ۖ

117
00:07:37,602 --> 00:07:39,508
It will be assigned from You; a miracle.

118
00:07:39,635 --> 00:07:43,542
وَارْزُقْنَا وَأَنتَ خَيْرُ الرَّازِقِينَ۝

119
00:07:44,055 --> 00:07:47,564
Provide for us sustenance; You Are the best of Sustainers.

120
00:07:48,497 --> 00:07:49,881
Al-Hawariyyeen(الحواريّين), they said;

121
00:07:49,971 --> 00:07:50,487
Number one;

122
00:07:50,507 --> 00:07:50,917
What?

123
00:07:51,097 --> 00:07:51,984
We want to eat.

124
00:07:52,404 --> 00:07:54,784
Sayidina Eesa(سيدنا عيسى) made it the last reason.

125
00:07:55,124 --> 00:07:55,751
وَارْزُقْنَا

126
00:07:55,771 --> 00:07:56,511
Give us Rizq(رزق).

127
00:07:56,804 --> 00:07:59,339
And Sayidina Eesa(سيدنا عيسى) did not limited to food.

128
00:07:59,806 --> 00:08:03,439
He did not say; Oh Allah! Give us this table to be food for us.

129
00:08:03,859 --> 00:08:06,597
Because food is only a very small part of Rizq(رزق).

130
00:08:06,744 --> 00:08:13,100
And Eesa(عيسى) made a comprehensive, and we learned from the Adiya(ادعیا) of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء); he made this comprehensive and said; Oh Allah! Give us Rizq(رزق).

131
00:08:14,147 --> 00:08:16,999
Not only limited to food on a table; give us Rizq(رزق).

132
00:08:17,139 --> 00:08:22,220
And Rizq(رزق) would include food, wealth, anything that you own, anything that you have.

133
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:26,717
Knowledge is also a form of Rizq(رزق); all of this is a Rizq(رزق) from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

134
00:08:27,236 --> 00:08:28,650
وَارْزُقْنَا وَأَنتَ خَيْرُ الرَّازِقِينَ۝

135
00:08:28,670 --> 00:08:30,835
Oh Allah! Give us and You Are the best of Providers.

136
00:08:31,055 --> 00:08:32,295
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said;

137
00:08:32,522 --> 00:08:36,432
قَالَ ٱللَّهُ إِنِّى مُنَزِّلُهَا عَلَيْكُمْ ۖ

138
00:08:36,512 --> 00:08:40,512
Allah said; I am going to send it down unto you; I will send it down.

139
00:08:41,185 --> 00:08:44,291
But Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

140
00:08:44,785 --> 00:08:54,812
فَمَن يَكْفُرْ بَعْدُ مِنكُمْ فَإِنِّىٓ أُعَذِّبُهُۥ عَذَابًا لَّآ أُعَذِّبُهُۥٓ أَحَدًا مِّنَ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ۝

141
00:08:55,059 --> 00:08:58,076
Allah says; I'm going to send it down unto you;

142
00:08:58,589 --> 00:09:08,947
but if any of you after that disbelieves; then I will punish him with a torment such as, I have not inflicted on anyone among all the world.

143
00:09:09,794 --> 00:09:17,116
When you ask for an Ayah(آية); when you ask for a miracle, and the miracle is performed, and then you disbelieve,

144
00:09:17,810 --> 00:09:20,643
it is worse than disbelieving without seeing a miracle.

145
00:09:21,196 --> 00:09:21,523
Why?

146
00:09:21,543 --> 00:09:26,965
Because you have asked Allah to provide you with a proof, and He provided you with the proof; nevertheless, you refused.

147
00:09:27,171 --> 00:09:33,784
And that's why, the more a person knows; the more a person is knowledgeable; the more responsible they become.

148
00:09:34,637 --> 00:09:40,822
 I mean, the responsibility on the scholar is greater than the responsibility on the layman, who has very limited information.

149
00:09:40,842 --> 00:09:41,336
Why?

150
00:09:41,496 --> 00:09:47,890
Because the scholar now, has many of the Ayaat(آيات) of Allah with him; which makes it, the greater obligation.

151
00:09:49,930 --> 00:09:54,836
And that's why, we know that the first three whom will be burnt in hellfire are who?

152
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:59,201
The scholar, and the Shaheed(شَهِيد), and who?

153
00:09:59,461 --> 00:10:02,121
And the man who spent a lot of money.

154
00:10:02,427 --> 00:10:03,067
Why?

155
00:10:03,227 --> 00:10:10,772
Because these are people who had signs of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, had Ni'mah(نِعْمَة) from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, and then they didn't use it right.

156
00:10:10,952 --> 00:10:12,559
The scholar used it to show off.

157
00:10:13,226 --> 00:10:16,987
And the Shaheed(شَهِيد) was fighting not for the sake of Allah, but was fighting for what?

158
00:10:17,213 --> 00:10:17,867
For fame.

159
00:10:18,060 --> 00:10:22,643
And then the other person was being generous; just to show the person; the people that he is generous.

160
00:10:22,863 --> 00:10:28,191
When you have seen the sign from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; the obligation becomes greater.

161
00:10:29,124 --> 00:10:35,206
This is the story of Al-Maidah(المائدة), and most of the scholars agreed that the Maidah(مائدة) was sent down.

162
00:10:35,660 --> 00:10:38,620
Now, in some of the books of Tafseer(تفسير); the old books of Tafseer(تفسير);

163
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:43,076
they mentioned, for example; the type of food that came down.

164
00:10:43,576 --> 00:10:46,243
They said; it was a fish that came down from the sky.

165
00:10:46,976 --> 00:10:50,704
And the fish was surrounded by five loaves of bread.

166
00:10:51,084 --> 00:10:56,436
One bread had olives, and one bread had cheese, and Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! This is;

167
00:10:56,496 --> 00:10:57,403
عِلمٍ لا يَنفَع

168
00:10:57,676 --> 00:10:59,203
This is knowledge that does not benefit.

169
00:11:00,090 --> 00:11:07,392
And as the tradition, that we have been following throughout the series of the lives of the Prophet, that we stay away from;

170
00:11:07,412 --> 00:11:08,001
عِلمٍ لا يَنفَع

171
00:11:08,054 --> 00:11:10,455
We stay away from the things that are not verified.

172
00:11:10,988 --> 00:11:15,411
If something is not confirmed by the Ayah(آية) of Qur'an or the Hadith(حديث); we stay away from it.

173
00:11:15,897 --> 00:11:19,411
What's the use of knowing, whether it was fish or meat or olives or bread?

174
00:11:20,717 --> 00:11:21,410
What is the benefit?

175
00:11:21,510 --> 00:11:25,150
Qur'an did not mentioned it, because there is no use to knowing such information.

176
00:11:25,477 --> 00:11:25,809
And that is;

177
00:11:25,876 --> 00:11:26,516
ترف علم

178
00:11:26,569 --> 00:11:28,396
That is luxury of knowledge.

179
00:11:29,069 --> 00:11:29,416
And that is;

180
00:11:29,436 --> 00:11:30,219
عِلمٍ لا يَنفَع

181
00:11:30,265 --> 00:11:31,435
Knowledge that does not benefit.

182
00:11:32,189 --> 00:11:37,620
It is knowledge that would not make you ignorant if you don't know it; and knowledge that will not make you knowledgeable if you do know it.

183
00:11:37,980 --> 00:11:46,485
And there's a lot of stories that were attributed to Sayidina Eesa(سيدنا عيسى) that would fall under this category, and we're going to stay away from all of them.

184
00:11:46,665 --> 00:11:53,011
If it does not confirmed strongly by the Ayah(آية) of Qur'an or the Hadith(حديث); then it's better to refrain from it.

185
00:11:53,804 --> 00:11:54,171
 Why?

186
00:11:54,191 --> 00:12:01,919
Because Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Would not hide away from us knowledge, if it's beneficial for us, if it's going to provide us with; Huda(هدى); guidance.

187
00:12:03,032 --> 00:12:15,837
The Yahood(يهود) in the time of Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام; they rejected the message of Eesa(عيسى), and a very small group believed in him.

188
00:12:15,884 --> 00:12:16,964
And these were Al-Hawariyyeen(الحواريّين).

189
00:12:16,997 --> 00:12:27,630
The rest of the community; whether it was the community itself, which were the jews, or the authorities, which were the Romans; they rejected the message of Eesaعليه السلام.

190
00:12:27,790 --> 00:12:34,169
The Jews plotted against Eesa(عيسى), and they conspired against him, with the government.

191
00:12:34,749 --> 00:12:40,415
They made a plot with the government, to assassinate and get rid of Sayidina Eesa(سيدنا عيسى).

192
00:12:40,835 --> 00:12:46,095
And the Roman authorities joined with the Yahood(يهود) in that conspiracy.

193
00:12:46,548 --> 00:12:54,839
The Yahood(يهود) are the ones who instigated it and then the Jews actually use the Romans to perform that plot against Sayidina Eesa(سيدنا عيسى).

194
00:12:55,359 --> 00:13:07,536
And the decree was issued that, Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام should be executed in public, by carrying him over the cross, and putting a crown over his head.

195
00:13:08,096 --> 00:13:10,376
Not the crown of gold or silver; but thorns.

196
00:13:11,216 --> 00:13:14,195
And to nail him to the cross, and let him bleed till death.

197
00:13:14,808 --> 00:13:18,221
And that was a very gruesome way of execution that they used to do.

198
00:13:18,441 --> 00:13:20,495
They would make a cross out of wood.

199
00:13:20,681 --> 00:13:25,480
And then, they would nail the hands and the feet to the cross.

200
00:13:25,527 --> 00:13:33,328
They would hit nails in the hands, and hang you on the cross and you would bleed from this injury from your feet and your hands until you die.

201
00:13:33,714 --> 00:13:38,509
And you could stay for hours and hours in the sun on that cross; dying a very slow death.

202
00:13:38,843 --> 00:13:41,255
So it was a very gruesome way of execution.

203
00:13:41,395 --> 00:13:45,468
So the law has been decreed that, Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام should be executed.

204
00:13:45,688 --> 00:13:48,540
We don't know the exact details of what happened.

205
00:13:48,560 --> 00:13:54,055
But there is a narration by Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) and again; I'm not sure of the authenticity of this narration.

206
00:13:54,955 --> 00:13:56,968
So we don't approve it or disapprove it.

207
00:13:57,848 --> 00:14:06,054
But it says that Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام ran into a room where all of his Hawariyyeen(حواريّين) were sitting.

208
00:14:06,420 --> 00:14:13,263
And then he told them; who will volunteer to sacrifice their life for me.

209
00:14:13,803 --> 00:14:18,486
One of the young, Hawariyyeen(حواريّين) raised up his hand and said; I will!

210
00:14:20,079 --> 00:14:27,102
Eesaعليه السلام asked another time; he's the only one who responded, he asked for a third time; that young man was the only one who responded.

211
00:14:28,308 --> 00:14:33,634
And this sacrifice is similar to what Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) did, when Rasool Allah ﷺ was in Al-Hijrah(هجرة).

212
00:14:35,214 --> 00:14:38,692
And incidentally enough, Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was young at that time.

213
00:14:38,972 --> 00:14:45,635
This young man came out, and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى put on him the resemblance of Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام.

214
00:14:45,782 --> 00:14:47,835
And he was the one who was crucified.

215
00:14:48,075 --> 00:14:58,194
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى opened for Eesa(عيسى) a window in the roof, and he was picked up by the angels safely and elevated to the heavens.

216
00:14:58,527 --> 00:15:00,007
This is one story.

217
00:15:00,207 --> 00:15:06,618
The other story is that, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى put the resemblance on one of the Jews who was an enemy of Sayidina Eesa(سيدنا عيسى).

218
00:15:07,185 --> 00:15:10,394
So Allah put the resemblance on him, and he was the one who was hanged on the cross.

219
00:15:11,307 --> 00:15:16,273
Regardless of who was hanged on the cross; it is not Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم).

220
00:15:17,393 --> 00:15:20,459
That is, what we are sure about; It was not Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم).

221
00:15:21,286 --> 00:15:23,670
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says in Surat Al-Imran(آلعمران);

222
00:15:24,063 --> 00:15:31,047
وَمَكَرُواْ وَمَكَرَ ٱللَّهُ ۖ وَٱللَّهُ خَيْرُ ٱلْمَٰكِرِينَ۝

223
00:15:31,507 --> 00:15:39,668
And they disbelievers plotted to kill Eesa(عيسى), and Allah plotted too; and Allah Is the best of those, who plot.

224
00:15:40,175 --> 00:15:47,990
Makar(مَكَر) means; when you plan in secret; when you're whispering; hiding in a room making a plan, that is called Makar(مَكَر).

225
00:15:48,703 --> 00:15:50,666
They think that they are doing Makar(مَكَر).

226
00:15:51,279 --> 00:15:55,399
They think that they're concealing their plan, and nobody knows their plan.

227
00:15:55,946 --> 00:15:59,091
But there is one who knows their plan, and that is Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

228
00:15:59,411 --> 00:16:00,941
Allah knows their plan so Allah is;

229
00:16:00,961 --> 00:16:01,741
خَيْرُ ٱلْمَٰكِرِينَ۝

230
00:16:01,944 --> 00:16:03,347
Allah Is the best of plotters.

231
00:16:03,593 --> 00:16:08,920
Because Allah; when He makes His plan; His plan can be secret and concealed, if Allah doesn't want anybody to know it.

232
00:16:09,380 --> 00:16:11,868
So they made their plan; but Allah made His plan.

233
00:16:11,928 --> 00:16:15,162
And the plan of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is what we'll go through.

234
00:16:15,468 --> 00:16:19,523
إِذْ قَالَ اللَّهُ يَا عِيسَىٰ إِنِّي مُتَوَفِّيكَ

235
00:16:19,803 --> 00:16:24,222
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said; Oh Eesa(عيسى)! I Will take you.

236
00:16:24,422 --> 00:16:25,262
مُتَوَفِّيكَ

237
00:16:25,768 --> 00:16:30,780
Many who read this Ayah(آية) think that Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) died.

238
00:16:30,987 --> 00:16:31,654
Why?

239
00:16:31,947 --> 00:16:34,474
Because the word Wafa(وَفَى) in Arabic means, death.

240
00:16:35,927 --> 00:16:38,042
Tuwuffi(تُوَفِّىْ) means; he died.

241
00:16:38,322 --> 00:16:39,609
Wafa(وَفَى) is death.

242
00:16:40,242 --> 00:16:40,862
So, when Allah says;

243
00:16:40,882 --> 00:16:41,976
إِنِّي مُتَوَفِّيكَ

244
00:16:42,629 --> 00:16:47,192
When people read this, they think that Allah Is telling Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) that; I Will make you die.

245
00:16:47,819 --> 00:16:57,888
But that is caused because of not knowing the meanings of words, and not knowing the original meaning of a word.

246
00:16:58,628 --> 00:17:05,380
It is true that, in the Arabic language of today and the Arabic language of yesterday; the word Mutawaffik(مُتَوَفِّيكَ) can mean death.

247
00:17:06,773 --> 00:17:08,383
But it also has other meanings.

248
00:17:09,016 --> 00:17:12,651
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى refer to sleep as Wafa(وَفَى).

249
00:17:13,031 --> 00:17:13,911
So what does it mean?

250
00:17:14,105 --> 00:17:15,838
Does it mean death, or does it mean sleep?

251
00:17:15,978 --> 00:17:21,200
The word Wafa(وَفَى) also has another third meaning, and that is; to take something completely.

252
00:17:21,933 --> 00:17:22,967
وفيه الاجر

253
00:17:23,187 --> 00:17:23,767
When you say;

254
00:17:23,787 --> 00:17:24,427
وفيه الاجر

255
00:17:24,600 --> 00:17:25,913
Means pay him in full.

256
00:17:26,606 --> 00:17:34,313
Over here the word Wafa(وَفَى) means; Allah's telling Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم); I Am going to take you in full, without any single injury.

257
00:17:35,386 --> 00:17:37,319
You are going to be taken entirely.

258
00:17:37,853 --> 00:17:39,778
You're not going to be harmed at all.

259
00:17:40,138 --> 00:17:42,698
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Is not going to take your soul alone.

260
00:17:43,285 --> 00:17:45,754
Nor Is Allahسُبحانه وتعالى going to take your body alone.

261
00:17:45,881 --> 00:17:51,296
Allah Is going to take your soul and your body intact without any injury or harm.

262
00:17:51,456 --> 00:17:54,630
That is what the word, Mutawaffika(مُتَوَفِّيكَ) means in this Ayah(آية).

263
00:17:55,290 --> 00:17:59,362
And this is actually the original meaning of the word Wafa(وَفَى).

264
00:17:59,596 --> 00:18:04,152
When we use Wafa(وَفَى) for death, or when we use it for sleeping;

265
00:18:04,339 --> 00:18:10,424
we're using secondary meanings of the word, but the original meaning is; something in its entirety or completely.

266
00:18:10,684 --> 00:18:16,383
And that's why, the word absolutely fits; The meaning which we want to get from the Ayah(آية);

267
00:18:16,563 --> 00:18:19,670
that the Yahood(يهود) were not able to harm Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم).

268
00:18:21,043 --> 00:18:22,236
وَرَافِعُكَ إِلَيَّ

269
00:18:22,429 --> 00:18:24,256
And I Will elevate you to me.

270
00:18:24,716 --> 00:18:27,083
وَمُطَهِّرُكَ مِنَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا

271
00:18:27,503 --> 00:18:33,885
And I Will purify you and clear you, of those who disbelieve.

272
00:18:34,292 --> 00:18:41,651
I Will clear you and purify you; take you away from all of this impurity; all of this Najasah(نجاسة); all of this Rijs(رجس);

273
00:18:42,178 --> 00:18:45,198
this environment that you're living in, I Will take you away from it.

274
00:18:45,951 --> 00:18:54,287
Now just to confirm the meaning further, we'll read Ayaat(آيات) from Surat Al-Nisa(سورت النساء), Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

275
00:18:55,001 --> 00:18:57,987
and these Ayaat(آيات) are talking about Al-Yahood(اليهود).

276
00:18:58,181 --> 00:19:07,449
Because of their breaking the covenant, and of their rejection of the Ayaat(آيات) of Allah, and of their killing the prophets unjustly,

277
00:19:07,795 --> 00:19:10,545
and of their saying; our hearts are wrapped,

278
00:19:11,085 --> 00:19:16,930
may Allah Has set a seal upon their hearts, because of their disbelief, so they believe not but a little.

279
00:19:17,143 --> 00:19:23,706
And because of their disbelief and uttering against Maryam(مريم) a grave false charge,

280
00:19:24,186 --> 00:19:32,088
and because of their saying in boast; We killed Messiah, Eesa(عيسى) the son of Mary, the Messenger of Allah.

281
00:19:32,342 --> 00:19:41,751
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; But they killed him not, nor crucified Him, but the resemblance of Eesa(عيسى) was put over another man.

282
00:19:42,804 --> 00:19:45,732
And those who differ therein are full of doubts.

283
00:19:46,292 --> 00:19:51,695
They have no certain knowledge; they follow nothing but conjecture.

284
00:19:52,202 --> 00:19:58,161
For surely they killed him not but Allah raised him up unto himself.

285
00:19:58,415 --> 00:20:00,648
And Allah is ever All Powerful, All Wise.

286
00:20:01,021 --> 00:20:06,357
And Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! When you read the Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an, and you look deeply into the words.

287
00:20:07,091 --> 00:20:09,644
Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! You find the miracle of Qur'an.

288
00:20:09,864 --> 00:20:20,383
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said in this issue in particular, in the issue of the crucifixion, and the killing of Eesa(عيسى), Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Is saying that;

289
00:20:20,423 --> 00:20:21,983
they're following nothing but doubts.

290
00:20:22,583 --> 00:20:29,182
If you go back to the Bible, and you look at the evidences that are used to prove that Eesa(عيسى) was crucified,

291
00:20:29,529 --> 00:20:36,145
and that he was killed, and that he was raised up from the dead; you find that all of those evidences are doubtful.

292
00:20:36,918 --> 00:20:40,941
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى summed it all in one word and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

293
00:20:41,007 --> 00:20:42,114
إِن يَتَّبِعُونَ إِلَّا الظَّنَّ ۖ

294
00:20:42,797 --> 00:20:44,921
They are following doubts; Shak(شك).

295
00:20:45,667 --> 00:20:52,222
Shak(شك) is doubtful, conjecture, there is no firm substantial evidence to prove the point.

296
00:20:52,489 --> 00:20:55,051
The life of Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام is not over.

297
00:20:55,551 --> 00:20:56,731
He's alive now.

298
00:20:58,011 --> 00:20:59,943
And the rest of his life is in the future.

299
00:21:00,323 --> 00:21:02,076
But we're not going to talk about it now.

300
00:21:02,349 --> 00:21:08,646
We'll keep it to the series about Al Akhirah(الآخرة) which we're going to start talking about In Sha' Allah(ان شاء الله) next Saturday.

301
00:21:08,706 --> 00:21:13,704
We started already with Al Akhirah(الآخرة) on Ramadan(رمضان), and we're going to continue In Sha' Allah(ان شاء الله) next Saturday.

302
00:21:14,010 --> 00:21:21,276
So we'll reserve the part about the Second Coming back of Eesa(عيسى) until, we talk about Alamat As-Sa'ah(علامت السّآئه).

303
00:21:21,562 --> 00:21:28,742
But up to this point, we are done with the history of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء); we're done with the past part of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

304
00:21:29,268 --> 00:21:35,253
Now, a few points that we will close with, in regards the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

305
00:21:35,826 --> 00:21:41,737
First of all; humanity and mankind; they need the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah.

306
00:21:41,977 --> 00:21:49,783
Mankind; they cannot live and survive without the Rusul(رُسُل), without the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء), without the messengers.

307
00:21:50,250 --> 00:21:56,555
 And I want to read to you some of the words of Ibn Al Qayyimرَحْمَةُ الله عَلَيه in this regards.

308
00:21:56,702 --> 00:21:57,415
He says;

309
00:21:57,935 --> 00:22:03,053
فإنه لا سبيل إلى السعادة والفلاح في الدنيا، ولا في الآخرة إلا على أيدي الرسل،

310
00:22:03,193 --> 00:22:11,096
 ولا سبيلَ إلى معرفة الطيب والخبيث على التفصيل إلا مِن جهتهم، ولا يُنال رضا الله البتة إلا على أيديهم،

311
00:22:11,629 --> 00:22:16,287
 فالطَّيِّب من الأعمال والأقوال والأخلاق، ليس إلا هديهم وما جاؤوا به،

312
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:22,391
 فهم الميزانُ الراجح الذي على أقوالهم وأخلاقهم تُوزن الأخلاق والأعمال،

313
00:22:22,825 --> 00:22:25,791
وبمتابعتهم يتميز أهل الضلال

314
00:22:26,305 --> 00:22:35,607
Ibn Al-Qayyim(إبنِ ألقَيِّم) says; There is no way to success and happiness in this world or in Akhirah(آخرة); except through the messengers.

315
00:22:36,160 --> 00:22:41,673
And there is no way to know the difference between good and evil; except through the messengers.

316
00:22:41,966 --> 00:22:47,836
And there is no way to receive the pleasure of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; except through the messengers.

317
00:22:48,076 --> 00:22:52,475
And then he says; They are the standard in their words and their actions.

318
00:22:52,695 --> 00:22:54,862
They are the standard, they are the criteria.

319
00:22:55,255 --> 00:23:00,249
And without the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; our spirits and our bodies will be dead.

320
00:23:00,849 --> 00:23:08,564
When we say this; we don't only mean that, it is important for us to learn about the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

321
00:23:09,184 --> 00:23:15,535
But is meant is that, the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى should be our guidance in everything that we do, in every aspect of our life.

322
00:23:16,068 --> 00:23:18,462
And that would lead to number two.

323
00:23:19,242 --> 00:23:28,319
Number two is; there's no way for us, to know and learn the guidance of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) except through; the Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an.

324
00:23:28,826 --> 00:23:29,786
There is no other way.

325
00:23:30,033 --> 00:23:32,576
Where are you going to learn about the guidance of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء)?

326
00:23:32,729 --> 00:23:33,249
Where?

327
00:23:33,502 --> 00:23:35,176
What other sources will you go back to?

328
00:23:35,389 --> 00:23:36,450
Historical books?

329
00:23:36,590 --> 00:23:38,097
History was not recorded yet.

330
00:23:38,817 --> 00:23:40,646
Are you going to go back to the Bible?

331
00:23:41,399 --> 00:23:47,427
Well let's look for example, at some of the references that were made in the Bible about the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى

332
00:23:47,447 --> 00:23:50,154
to see if we can use it as a credible source.

333
00:23:50,794 --> 00:24:00,378
The Bible says about Nuh(نوح), and these by the way, all of these verses that I will read are from the Old Testament which is part of the Jews.

334
00:24:00,724 --> 00:24:01,904
Now this is talking about Nuh(نوح).

335
00:24:02,064 --> 00:24:07,324
Noah; a man of the soil, proceeded to plant a vine yard.

336
00:24:08,264 --> 00:24:15,083
When he drank some of its wine; he became drunk, and lay uncovered inside his tent.

337
00:24:15,963 --> 00:24:24,443
Ham; the father of the father of Can'an saw his father's nakedness, and told his two brothers outside.

338
00:24:24,616 --> 00:24:31,748
But Chen and Japheth took a garment and laid it across their shoulders.

339
00:24:32,135 --> 00:24:35,730
Then they walked in backward and covered their father's nakedness.

340
00:24:35,904 --> 00:24:41,470
Their faces were turned the other way, so that they would not see their father's nakedness.

341
00:24:41,983 --> 00:24:48,288
When Noah awoke from his wine, and found out what his youngest son has done to him.

342
00:24:48,308 --> 00:24:53,394
He said; Cursed be Can'an, the lowest of slaves, will he be to his brothers.

343
00:24:53,927 --> 00:24:56,677
And this is in Genesis 920.

344
00:24:57,231 --> 00:25:02,037
About Sayidina Ibrahimعليه السلام Exodus 31, verse one.

345
00:25:02,637 --> 00:25:15,663
It mentions that Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم), used his wife Sarah(ساره) to go to the king of Egypt, so that he can gain some material gains.

